      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brock was founded in 1854 by George Shroaf near the Nemaha River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village has had many names—Shroaf’s Ford, Bradley’s Bridge, Pinhook, Clinton, Dayton, Howard, and Podunk—before settling on Brock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the Missouri Pacific railroad planned a line across the prairie, Brock was platted in 1878 and the depot was built in 1881.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://enjoynemahacounty.org/brock/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A crude dam and grist mill powered by the Nemaha River’s waterfall were erected in 1867, followed by a sawmill in 1870.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://enjoynemahacounty.org/brock/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first general store opened on the south side of the river in 1871, marking the start of commercial activity.",
